    {
      "id": 147381,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-09-10T03:08:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"VisforYoshi\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/visforyoshi/48/2185_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> VisforYoshi:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I like to collect old cook books, usually from garage/yard sales. Not only are the recipes in them usually really good, but it's really cool to look through. Like a more interesting history book.My favorite one so far is a collection of recipes from recovering alcoholics that came from the 70s.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I love old recipe books. &nbsp;Since I've moved to Pittsburgh I've been working on old parish cookbooks from the ethnic neighborhoods. &nbsp;Those recipes are awesome.</p>\n<p>I'm much more about the recipe than the books though, I get a food in mind and have to find the right recipe that gives me exactly what I want from that food.</p>\n<p>Alcohol is quickly catching up, drink recipes and finding the best liquer for the drinks I like is becoming an obsession.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:25:28.299Z",
